@page "/docs/components/attachment"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Attachment
<PageTitle>Attachment - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Attachment</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="attachment" />
        </div>
        <p>File cards that show upload progress, plus a drag-and-drop zone to collect the files. The dropzone runs no JavaScript: a native file input stretched across it handles clicks, the keyboard and files dropped from the operating system, and it checks type, size and count for you. Each card is composed from media, a title and description, optional actions and an optional full-card trigger.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(AttachmentDefaultExample)" />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Dropzone" Description="Drag files onto the zone, which highlights while you hover, or click it to browse. Accepted files arrive through `OnFilesAccepted`, and files that break the `Accept`, `MaxFileSize` or `MaxFiles` limits are reported through `OnFilesRejected`."
          Example="typeof(AttachmentDropzoneExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Image" Description="Set `Orientation` to `Vertical` to stack the card, so an image preview fills the top."
          Example="typeof(AttachmentImageExample)" />

    <Demo Title="States" Description="`State` follows the upload lifecycle. `Uploading` and `Processing` pulse the media and mute the title, `Error` turns the border and description destructive, and `Done` returns the card to rest."
          Example="typeof(AttachmentStatesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Sizes" Description="`Size` offers three densities: `Default`, `Sm`, and a chip-like `Xs`."
          Example="typeof(AttachmentSizesExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Group" Description="`BzAttachmentGroup` lines cards up in a horizontally scrollable row, which suits message composers and upload trays."
          Example="typeof(AttachmentGroupExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Trigger" Description="`BzAttachmentTrigger` lays an invisible overlay across the card so the whole surface is clickable, here opening a preview dialog. The card's actions sit above it and stay independently clickable."
          Example="typeof(AttachmentTriggerExample)" />

</div>
